      "url": "https://boingboing.net/2026/08/02/red-bull-funded-energy-drink-research.html",
      "title": "Red Bull paid for the studies saying vodka Red Bulls are fine",
      "content_html": "<a href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/08/02/red-bull-funded-energy-drink-research.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Red Bull paid for the studies saying vodka Red Bulls are fine\"><img alt=\"Red Bull funded research — MoserB / CC0 (Wikimedia Commons)\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"1028\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/boingboing.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/1280px-Red_Bull_in_Israel.jpg?fit=1280%2C1028&amp;quality=60&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 5px;\" width=\"1280\" /></a><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of the studies on mixing alcohol and energy drinks funded by Red Bull or written by researchers with financial ties to it, 95% found no added risk. Roughly 80% of independent studies found the opposite, <a href=\"https://www.theexamination.org/articles/red-bull-funded-research-energy-drinks-alcohol\">The Examination reports</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At a February 2011 hearing in Suffolk County, New York, Dutch researcher Joris Verster likened blaming energy drinks for alcohol-fueled injuries to blaming shark attacks on ice cream sales. &#8212; <a class=\"read-more\" href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/08/02/red-bull-funded-energy-drink-research.html\">Read the rest </a></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://boingboing.net/2026/08/02/red-bull-funded-energy-drink-research.html\">Red Bull paid for the studies saying vodka Red Bulls are fine</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://boingboing.net\">Boing Boing</a>.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-08-02T17:10:08+00:00",
